{"id": "EUVD-2026-105311", "enisaUuid": "68e16f98-6ec4-330a-b97a-64d6c39fde93", "description": "An authenticated HTTPS origin can supply an HSTS `max-age` value that the\nparser accepts, but time serialization later fails to process. On 64-bit\nsystems, extreme max-age values compute an absolute expiry within standard\ntime integer limits that exceeds calendar time structure bounds. During cache\nsaves, the original HSTS file is truncated before writing a temporary\nreplacement; when serialization fails, the temporary file is deleted, leaving\nan empty or partial cache. Because the save error is silently ignored during\ncleanup, curl exits successfully despite the data loss.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T20:13:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T20:13:22", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://curl.se/docs/CVE-2026-87863.json", "https://curl.se/docs/CVE-2026-87863.html", "https://hackerone.com/reports/3972373"], "aliases": ["GHSA-53q4-87wj-266h", "CVE-2026-87863"], "assigner": "curl", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03bd0cc2-77c6-3c26-80d7-a074127deae1", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.17.0 \u22648.17.0"}, {"id": "0fda4709-15eb-3158-bcf4-9193c89e53c3", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.21.0 \u22648.21.0"}, {"id": "1deb2266-df6d-3bfd-9beb-cc1cf4416e70", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.3.0 \u22648.3.0"}, {"id": "29113469-ef45-318c-9bc4-d9b913178762", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.11.0 \u22648.11.0"}, {"id": "2d479cf3-9776-347f-8d33-9ce032b1d364", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.7.1 \u22648.7.1"}, {"id": "3b26e99c-2344-3ec1-8f3e-1c9bf27fa808", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.2.1 \u22648.2.1"}, {"id": "4c040ad7-5c7c-39fe-a1c4-d3cba2a2d5fd", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"nam